# OpenSocrates for Cursor

This package is the experimental, content-only Cursor Agent Plugin for
OpenSocrates {{PRODUCT_VERSION}}. It exposes one `opensocrates` Agent Skill
backed by {{METHOD_COUNT}} internal reasoning-system references.

When the skill reads a generated method, that complete procedure begins with
three authored teacher questions for the active agent to settle without
unnecessarily interviewing the user. This is content-only skill behavior, not
an OpenSocrates hook claim.

## Support boundary

- Manual `/opensocrates` invocation: implemented through Cursor's documented
  Agent Plugin and Agent Skills contracts; a live Cursor receipt is pending.
- Cursor's built-in agent-decided skill discovery: host-owned behavior; no
  separate OpenSocrates selector model call is added.
- OpenSocrates automatic per-prompt hook selection: not included.
- Native hook delivery, local records, and deterministic trace rendering: not
  claimed.

There is no launcher, native runtime, executable, hook, MCP server, telemetry,
background service, or additional model process in this package.

## Local plugin contract

Cursor documents local development plugins under
`~/.cursor/plugins/local/<plugin-name>/`. Agent Plugins use a root
`plugin.json`; skills live under `skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`. After
installation, reload Cursor and invoke `/opensocrates` from Agent chat.

See Cursor's [Plugins documentation](https://cursor.com/docs/plugins) and
[Agent Skills documentation](https://cursor.com/docs/skills).

